WEBVTT

00:02:28.811 --> 00:02:30.897
Humans are creative omnivores.

00:02:30.897 --> 00:02:33.691
We can get calcium
from a lot of other sources --

00:02:33.733 --> 00:02:35.401
yogurt and cheese, for example --

00:02:35.401 --> 00:02:38.946
but also look for leafy greens
like spinach and kale,

00:02:38.946 --> 00:02:41.866
cruciferous vegetables
like broccoli and cabbage,

00:02:41.866 --> 00:02:45.661
and proteins like tofu,
nuts, beans, eggs and fish.

00:02:45.661 --> 00:02:49.081
Fortified cereals and orange juice
are also good too,

00:02:49.123 --> 00:02:50.249
and chia seeds.

00:02:50.291 --> 00:02:53.085
And vitamin D
is plentiful in fatty fishes,

00:02:53.085 --> 00:02:55.129
and our skin makes it from the sun.

00:02:55.171 --> 00:02:57.465
However, some people may need supplements.

00:02:57.506 --> 00:03:00.468
Another important factor
for bone health is exercise.